From: "Barak A. Pearlmutter" <barak+git@pearlmutter.net>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 13:50:00 +0100
Subject: store settings under ~/.config/DiffPDF

Settings were stored under ~/.config/Qtrac Ltd./, named after the
original author's company, which is neither obvious nor appropriate now
that the free version is maintained by others.  Use DiffPDF as the
organization name, copy any existing settings from the old location on
first run, and document the file in the man page.

Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/767157
Forwarded: no
---
 diffpdf.1.cmake |  7 +++++++
 main.cpp        | 12 +++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 18 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/diffpdf.1.cmake b/diffpdf.1.cmake
index 8f7cf31..c85d93f 100644
--- a/diffpdf.1.cmake
+++ b/diffpdf.1.cmake
@@ -26,6 +26,13 @@ second. This will make DiffPDF compare pages in the pairs (1, 1), (2,
 If the program is passed two PDF filenames on the command line it will
 start up and compare those files in Text mode (or in Appearance mode if
 the filenames are preceded by \-a or \-\-appearance).
+.SH FILES
+.TP
+.I ~/.config/DiffPDF/DiffPDF.conf
+User settings (window layout, zoom, margins, highlighting, etc.).
+Older versions stored these in
+.IR "~/.config/Qtrac Ltd./DiffPDF.conf" ,
+from which they are copied the first time a newer version is run.
 .SH "SEE ALSO"
 For a command line tool for comparing PDF files see
 http://www.qtrac.eu/comparepdf.html.
diff --git a/main.cpp b/main.cpp
index 94c2a25..e9b5052 100644
--- a/main.cpp
+++ b/main.cpp
@@ -27,9 +27,19 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[])
 #ifdef Q_WS_MAC
     app.setCursorFlashTime(0);
 #endif
-    app.setOrganizationName("Qtrac Ltd.");
+    app.setOrganizationName("DiffPDF");
     app.setOrganizationDomain("qtrac.eu");
     app.setApplicationName("DiffPDF");
+    {
+        // Settings used to live under the original author's company
+        // name; carry them over the first time we run.
+        QSettings settings;
+        if (settings.allKeys().isEmpty()) {
+            QSettings old("Qtrac Ltd.", "DiffPDF");
+            foreach (const QString &key, old.allKeys())
+                settings.setValue(key, old.value(key));
+        }
+    }
     app.setWindowIcon(QIcon(":/icon.png"));
 
     QTextStream out(stdout);
